WEBVTT

00:03.780 --> 00:08.780
<i>Appeared a spider in the capital long, long ago.</i>

00:08.780 --> 00:10.750
<i>And caused harm to mankind it did.</i>

00:11.170 --> 00:13.560
In plain language, please?

00:17.130 --> 00:18.370
Help!

00:32.010 --> 00:34.000
It's coming! Aim!

02:17.900 --> 02:22.870
Kokumondo

02:22.870 --> 02:24.700
Look!

02:24.700 --> 02:27.880
I don't care about the contents of the book.

02:29.650 --> 02:31.580
That's no good, Mizuki.

02:31.580 --> 02:32.570
Unacceptable!

02:32.570 --> 02:33.340
What is?

02:33.340 --> 02:37.760
Is that how a person who's thrown herself
into the world of historic books should talk?

02:37.760 --> 02:38.890
Is it?

02:38.890 --> 02:40.220
But I didn't!

02:40.670 --> 02:44.140
I came here in place of my grandpa to collect this month's rent!

02:48.240 --> 02:51.370
A book with a monster sealed inside, huh?

02:51.370 --> 02:53.280
Huh? Wait! Clean your hands!

02:53.280 --> 02:55.030
Put on some gloves!

03:02.210 --> 03:03.250
...whoops.

03:07.980 --> 03:11.950
Hi. This is Suzuri from Kokumondou.

03:09.960 --> 03:12.790
Closed

03:12.330 --> 03:14.150
Yes, yes.

03:12.790 --> 03:15.210
Monster Spider Tale

03:14.150 --> 03:15.210
I have the item.

03:16.000 --> 03:16.890
Yes.

03:17.260 --> 03:20.040
Oh, it wasn't easy.

03:20.040 --> 03:22.670
I tried everything I could.

03:22.670 --> 03:27.520
By the way, I wanted to talk to you about the condition of the book.

03:28.770 --> 03:29.490
What?

03:29.850 --> 03:32.480
No, nothing like that!

03:32.480 --> 03:33.980
Yes, yes.

03:34.790 --> 03:35.900
Oh, no.

03:36.980 --> 03:38.450
Cockroach?

03:38.580 --> 03:39.570
Is it a cockroach?!

03:47.450 --> 03:49.660
Oh, my, my!

03:49.660 --> 03:52.740
Mizuki, Mr. Saki is infuriated.

03:56.430 --> 03:57.800
Icky harry!

03:57.800 --> 03:59.380
What are you talking about?

03:59.380 --> 04:01.990
Something's here! It's big and creepy!

04:01.990 --> 04:03.930
Can you please check?

04:03.930 --> 04:05.550
You're overreacting.

04:05.550 --> 04:07.890
It's probably just a mouse or a cricket.

04:07.890 --> 04:09.220
A cricket?!

04:32.660 --> 04:35.890
I need to organize my collections.

04:39.840 --> 04:40.710
I heard a cry!

04:40.710 --> 04:41.940
Something cried!

04:41.940 --> 04:43.050
I heard a "kee"!

04:50.510 --> 04:53.190
And not a single concern for my well-being.

04:53.190 --> 04:53.910
Hm?

04:55.940 --> 04:56.850
What was this again?

05:04.430 --> 05:05.890
A doll?

05:05.890 --> 05:07.530
I don't recall having one.

05:14.290 --> 05:15.410
It moved!

05:15.410 --> 05:16.210
What is that?

05:16.610 --> 05:17.690
What is that thing?

05:17.690 --> 05:20.170
Wow, that's peculiar.

05:30.190 --> 05:31.390
Adorable.

05:33.050 --> 05:35.700
Why if it isn't just a deary little girl.

05:35.700 --> 05:36.480
Lovely!

05:36.480 --> 05:38.080
What a lovable girl.

05:38.080 --> 05:39.140
What?

05:39.140 --> 05:40.460
How?

05:40.460 --> 05:41.730
It's tiny!

05:41.730 --> 05:42.940
It's weird!

05:44.220 --> 05:44.940
Here.

06:10.470 --> 06:11.450
Ouch.

06:15.860 --> 06:19.060
It's a monster!

06:29.580 --> 06:32.340
The giant spider monster that attacked the capital

06:33.000 --> 06:36.160
fled after being hit with the onmyoji's sacred energy.

06:36.660 --> 06:42.660
Skulls and baby spider corpses trailed out of the monster's stomach.

06:42.660 --> 06:43.870
Gross.

06:44.610 --> 06:48.850
Among the corpses, they found one baby spider that resembled a human girl.

06:49.210 --> 06:50.840
O-Okay...

06:51.330 --> 06:55.470
The onmyoji tried to kill her too, but couldn't...

06:55.470 --> 06:56.520
He's a pedo?

06:57.140 --> 06:59.950
So took her home against everyone's wishes.

06:59.950 --> 07:01.450
He is!

07:05.270 --> 07:09.670
The onmyoji cared for the little spider girl like a normal human.

07:13.070 --> 07:19.140
But after six months time, the men at a
nearby village began to vanish one by one.

07:45.000 --> 07:47.610
I've finally got you cornered, spider beast!

07:47.610 --> 07:48.400
Prepare yourself!

07:48.400 --> 07:50.400
Spi-de-de-dee!

07:50.960 --> 07:52.860
Or so it says on the book.

07:53.200 --> 07:55.820
Wh-What a powerful image.

07:56.290 --> 07:58.920
It's written very realistically.

07:58.920 --> 08:01.920
So what happened in the end?

08:01.920 --> 08:02.810
I don't know.

08:02.810 --> 08:04.790
You don't? It's not on the book?

08:07.130 --> 08:09.190
It's blank...

08:09.190 --> 08:13.510
I'm sure originally, this page had the spider girl's end, but...

08:13.510 --> 08:15.510
Spi-de-dee!

08:26.230 --> 08:29.530
Suzuri, what are you gonna do with that?

08:29.530 --> 08:31.450
What is there to do?

08:31.450 --> 08:35.830
The seal broke, and it escaped out of the drawing.

08:35.830 --> 08:41.540
She probably won't go back in no matter how
much we ask her, look at her, or care for her.

08:42.030 --> 08:44.850
I can't sell a book with a page missing.

08:44.850 --> 08:47.260
Ergo I can't pay the rent,

08:47.260 --> 08:50.190
and your grandfather won't give you any allowance.

08:50.190 --> 08:51.460
We're hopeless.

08:51.460 --> 08:54.200
Don't give up so easily!

08:54.200 --> 08:56.770
I'm just a used book salesman.

08:56.770 --> 09:00.810
I can't seal a monster back into its book.

09:00.810 --> 09:01.770
But she eats-

09:04.270 --> 09:06.080
She eats people!

09:06.080 --> 09:07.020
What if she eats us?

09:08.640 --> 09:10.100
That's just a legend.

09:10.100 --> 09:11.850
A myth, so to speak.

09:11.850 --> 09:14.270
But the monster is really here!

09:14.270 --> 09:15.920
Don't worry.

09:15.920 --> 09:19.370
That cute little thing can't possibly do anything evi-

09:26.030 --> 09:26.670
Hey!

09:27.480 --> 09:29.400
That's not for you to eat.

10:01.480 --> 10:02.410
Suzuri!

10:10.310 --> 10:13.340
Did you figure anything out about the monster?

10:13.340 --> 10:16.890
I finally got in touch with my senior historic book expert.

10:16.890 --> 10:19.030
He said he'll lend us a hand.

10:19.030 --> 10:19.720
Really?

10:43.140 --> 10:45.260
She looks a little lonely.

10:49.230 --> 10:50.250
Mommy.

10:50.580 --> 10:52.170
I-It spoke!

11:06.840 --> 11:07.720
Suzuri?

11:14.820 --> 11:17.730
Geppoan

11:15.750 --> 11:17.730
Geppoan?

11:21.470 --> 11:25.370
Wow, that's peculiar.

11:26.090 --> 11:27.950
Why do they all react the same?

11:27.950 --> 11:30.210
Right? It's rare.

11:30.640 --> 11:33.160
I mean, a historic monster jumped out of the book!

11:33.160 --> 11:34.560
Aren't you jealous?

11:34.560 --> 11:36.770
Yeah, I am.

11:36.770 --> 11:40.920
Though you can't just keep it as your pet forever.

11:41.300 --> 11:43.250
Yes! That's exactly right!

11:43.250 --> 11:44.640
What? I can't?

11:46.170 --> 11:48.840
I was going to so long as she didn't mind.

11:48.840 --> 11:50.980
What? Are you an idiot?

11:50.980 --> 11:52.460
There's no way that's okay!

11:52.460 --> 11:53.430
Right?

11:55.720 --> 11:57.630
I was kidding.

11:57.630 --> 12:00.690
I'll be happy if there's some sane method we can use to put her back in that book.

12:09.850 --> 12:10.620
Here.

12:11.420 --> 12:14.760
It's the place mentioned in this book.

12:14.760 --> 12:17.560
This will probably give you a clue.

12:18.500 --> 12:19.770
Thank you.

12:20.260 --> 12:23.340
You can pay me back with something of equal value.

12:29.350 --> 12:30.810
Suzuri!

12:32.520 --> 12:34.210
Schoolgirl.

12:34.770 --> 12:38.150
How long has he been like that?

12:38.150 --> 12:39.400
Like what?

12:40.310 --> 12:43.150
Is it too late? Or...

12:48.630 --> 12:49.530
Yes?

13:00.770 --> 13:02.570
Let's go check it out!

13:02.570 --> 13:03.240
What?

13:03.240 --> 13:05.820
The place on that map!

13:06.580 --> 13:10.180
You heard what the monster said on the roof, didn't you?

13:11.520 --> 13:12.600
Yeah.

13:13.100 --> 13:14.860
She was calling for her mom!

13:14.860 --> 13:16.430
She wants to go home!

13:16.430 --> 13:18.790
I'm sure it's her home!

13:18.790 --> 13:20.400
Yeah, maybe, but...

13:20.900 --> 13:22.440
So let's go?

14:44.780 --> 14:47.010
It's... wow.

14:47.010 --> 14:50.460
It must've been quite an extraordinary place back in that age.

14:52.220 --> 14:54.240
Let's let her see this too.

14:58.520 --> 15:00.550
Hey, that tickles.

15:00.550 --> 15:02.020
There, there.

15:03.250 --> 15:05.920
Okay, let's go!

15:09.070 --> 15:10.160
There.

15:10.580 --> 15:11.340
How's that?

15:11.340 --> 15:15.970
If the legend is really true...

16:11.620 --> 16:14.280
Hey, what's gotten into you all of a sudden?

16:14.780 --> 16:16.740
Okay, hold on.

16:19.200 --> 16:20.120
Suzuri!

16:20.830 --> 16:21.410
Hm?

16:25.790 --> 16:27.060
Wait!

17:01.260 --> 17:03.490
Hey!

17:04.840 --> 17:06.790
Where are you?

17:10.390 --> 17:12.130
Suzuri!

17:20.340 --> 17:22.630
Come out!

17:40.470 --> 17:42.400
Suzuri! Wait!

17:42.400 --> 17:43.430
Suzuri!

17:55.110 --> 17:57.480
He can't be caught in the web.

17:57.480 --> 18:03.560
Return the monster to where it belongs, then get Suzuri back!

18:04.460 --> 18:06.290
Easier said than done.

18:20.840 --> 18:22.720
Don't worry.

18:24.110 --> 18:25.750
Where are you?

18:28.120 --> 18:30.330
You don't need to run away.

18:33.510 --> 18:34.620
Come.

18:49.440 --> 18:51.000
Please! Don't go after her!

18:51.900 --> 18:54.070
What are you saying?

18:54.640 --> 18:56.720
You have to stop, Suzuri!

18:56.720 --> 18:58.070
You won't be able to come back!

19:01.360 --> 19:02.620
You see-

19:05.320 --> 19:07.250
Th-This web...

19:12.990 --> 19:14.250
Suzuri!

19:19.420 --> 19:22.320
You can't go! You just can't!

19:48.500 --> 19:50.080
M-Mizuki?

19:51.180 --> 19:53.540
Suzuri, you're back.

19:55.060 --> 19:57.440
What's... going on?

19:57.440 --> 20:01.510
The old man from Geppoan said to rewind the web to something else before you got sucked in.

20:02.940 --> 20:06.320
But who would rewind it to the main pillar?!

20:06.320 --> 20:07.720
But...

20:17.520 --> 20:18.580
What's that?

20:32.080 --> 20:33.420
A giant spider?!

20:58.520 --> 21:00.680
Wh-What is this?

21:11.620 --> 21:12.910
Mommy.

22:19.400 --> 22:20.520
Good day.

22:23.090 --> 22:24.020
Here.

22:24.380 --> 22:26.340
Thank you for this map.

22:27.170 --> 22:27.990
Sure.

22:29.560 --> 22:31.910
And you...

22:31.910 --> 22:34.950
Well, you see.

22:35.530 --> 22:37.570
A lot happened.

22:41.820 --> 22:43.210
Tea is served.

22:43.210 --> 22:44.800
Oh, thanks.

22:51.940 --> 22:54.940
Well, you know...

22:55.610 --> 22:59.660
I guess I better give you a discount.

22:59.660 --> 23:00.940
Thank you, sir.

